course: dictionary
lesson: 10250
title: Words in a graveyard: tombstone
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tombstone is a large stone at a grave, with the name of the person buried there and often words about them. «The name was carved on the tombstone.» The words around tombstone give clues: carved tells you the name was cut into the stone, and a grave tells you where it stands.
explain: Historians read old tombstones like clues from the past. In a churchyard, an old tombstone can tell you a person's name, their age and their family. «The old tombstone was covered in green moss.» Moss grows slowly, so the stone has been there a long time.
explain: A tombstone marks where someone is buried, and visiting is a way to remember them. Gravestone and headstone are other words for it. Visitors should be quiet and respectful, because the people buried there are resting.
explain: Words can be used in different ways. «Tombstoning» is a different word that uses tombstone, and it is not a game to copy. The clue is in the sentence: «Hitting rock, or even hitting water from high up, can break the back or neck; tombstoning has killed and paralysed people in the UK.» Always stay safe and ask an adult when you are unsure.
fact: A tombstone is a large stone over or at the end of a grave.
fact: A tombstone often has the name of the person buried there, and words about them.
fact: Gravestone and headstone are other words that mean much the same as tombstone.
fact: In films and games, tombstones are often used in spooky graveyard scenes.
fact: Historians can learn names, ages and families from old tombstones in churchyards.
exercise: «The old tombstone was covered in green moss.» What is a tombstone? | A soft cushion for sitting on | *A large stone over or at the end of a grave | A type of spooky film | A tall tree in a park
exercise: Lily visits a churchyard to remember her grandad. How should she behave? | Throwing stones at the tombstones | *Quiet and respectful | Loud and running between the graves | Climbing on the tombstones to see the view
exercise: Another word for tombstone is | blanket | *gravestone | castle | river
test: «The name was carved on the tombstone.» What was carved on the tombstone? | A shopping list | *The name of the person buried there | Today's weather | A picture of a dragon
test: The sentence says tombstoning is dangerous. What is the clue? | It is always quiet and calm | It is a recipe for a cake | *Hitting rock or water from high up can break the back or neck | It is the same as visiting a graveyard
exam: Why do historians read old tombstones? | To learn how to swim | *To learn the names, ages and families of people from the past | To find the best place to play football | To cook a special meal
